WEBVTT

00:02.709 --> 00:05.678
&lt;i>Ask your doctor if it's right for you.&lt;/i>

00:05.845 --> 00:10.009
So do you either of guys urinate
with abnormal frequency?

00:11.985 --> 00:14.010
- No.
- No.

00:15.722 --> 00:18.623
I mean, you gotta define abnormal.

00:18.791 --> 00:23.091
And keep in mind the body
doesn't process alcohol efficiently...

00:23.329 --> 00:26.423
...which is why your Uncle Charlie
is a perpetual urine machine.

00:27.066 --> 00:30.001
Also keep in mind that your father
has the bladder control...

00:30.170 --> 00:32.730
...of a frightened 9-year-old girl.

00:34.040 --> 00:37.874
Which is why he needs to wear
two pairs of undies and a pantyliner.

00:38.611 --> 00:40.476
Only on long drives.

00:40.647 --> 00:43.207
Really? How many times a night
do you get up to pee?

00:43.383 --> 00:45.681
- Just once.
- I can hear your toilet flush, Alan.

00:45.852 --> 00:47.877
Okay, four times.

00:48.054 --> 00:50.420
But at least I get out of bed to pee.

00:50.590 --> 00:53.286
Hey, hey,
that was an isolated incident.

00:53.493 --> 00:56.223
I was dreaming
my shoes were on fire.

00:56.396 --> 00:59.388
- Does that answer your question, buddy?
- Yeah.

00:59.566 --> 01:01.830
And remind me
to never to ask another one.

01:03.102 --> 01:05.002
- Charlie?
- Yeah?

01:05.605 --> 01:08.073
- Why aren't you ready?
- Ready for?

01:08.241 --> 01:10.038
You've gotta be kidding me.

01:10.210 --> 01:13.941
I've told you three times we're having
dinner with my girlfriend Gail tonight.

01:14.113 --> 01:15.944
Excuse me, gotta pee.

01:16.950 --> 01:20.750
You never listen when I'm talking to you.
It's like you just tune me out.

01:20.920 --> 01:24.117
You look like you're paying attention,
but your mind is miles away.

01:24.290 --> 01:25.655
&lt;i>Do I need to pee?&lt;/i>

01:27.994 --> 01:31.259
&lt;i>Nah. I mean, I could. Might be traffic.&lt;/i>

01:31.431 --> 01:33.831
&lt;i>Probably should pee. Yeah, better pee.&lt;/i>

01:34.000 --> 01:36.298
We're gonna be late,
I'm gonna be embarrassed...

01:36.469 --> 01:41.600
&lt;i>...because you don't listen.
- Boy, she's got great boobies.&lt;/i>

02:12.138 --> 02:14.936
So, Charlie, I've heard
so many nice things about you.

02:15.108 --> 02:16.837
Really? From who?

02:18.645 --> 02:20.203
Hello.

02:21.414 --> 02:23.644
Oh, right. Thanks.

02:23.816 --> 02:26.011
I guess I only hear the complaints.

02:27.654 --> 02:30.248
- You don't hear anything.
- That's not true.

02:30.423 --> 02:33.358
You're right, it's not.
He hears what he wants to hear.

02:34.627 --> 02:36.458
So I'm right.

02:38.131 --> 02:40.691
- Well, you still make a great couple.
- Thank you.

02:40.867 --> 02:43.665
And I'm really looking forward
to your wedding.

02:43.836 --> 02:45.326
I'm sure it's gonna be beautiful.

02:48.141 --> 02:49.631
What'd I do?

02:49.809 --> 02:52.300
Nothing. I told you,
she's going through a breakup.

02:52.478 --> 02:57.108
- When did you tell me that?
- In the car on the way here. God!

02:58.951 --> 03:00.714
It's gonna be okay.

03:00.887 --> 03:02.149
I know, it's just hard.

03:02.922 --> 03:04.321
I thought I knew him.

03:04.490 --> 03:07.982
I thought we were gonna be together
forever like you and Charlie.

03:08.528 --> 03:12.157
&lt;i>Hard to believe
somebody got tired of doing her.&lt;/i>

03:13.299 --> 03:16.166
&lt;i>Ooh. French fries look good.&lt;/i>

03:16.803 --> 03:19.863
&lt;i>Why did I order the baked potato?&lt;/i>

03:20.039 --> 03:23.099
- Isn't that right, Charlie?
- Absolutely.

03:23.710 --> 03:26.304
&lt;i>Now is this the one
who's the old college roommate?&lt;/i>

03:26.479 --> 03:28.538
&lt;i>I should really listen more.&lt;/i>

03:28.715 --> 03:30.808
I mean, I knew he was insensitive.

03:30.983 --> 03:35.010
&lt;i>Boy, I bet if they were roommates,
they did some experimenting.&lt;/i>

03:35.888 --> 03:38.982
&lt;i>Why is it that girls can experiment
with girls and not be gay...&lt;/i>

03:39.158 --> 03:42.184
&lt;i>... but if a guy so much kisses
another guy... Bad memory.&lt;/i>

03:42.362 --> 03:44.762
&lt;i>Drink, drink, drink, drink.&lt;/i>

03:45.465 --> 03:47.933
So you're just all alone
in that big apartment?

03:48.568 --> 03:51.002
- He even took the dog.
- Bastard.

03:51.170 --> 03:53.434
What? It's my first drink.

03:53.606 --> 03:56.803
- Not you. Brian took Rufus.
- Ohh.

03:57.043 --> 03:59.068
&lt;i>Who's Rufus?&lt;/i>

03:59.846 --> 04:01.507
&lt;i>For that matter, who's Brian?&lt;/i>

04:01.681 --> 04:04.479
&lt;i>Life of Brian, that was pretty funny.&lt;/i>

04:04.650 --> 04:06.880
&lt;i>Brian's Song not so much.&lt;/i>

04:07.720 --> 04:09.688
&lt;i>James Caan was great in it, though.&lt;/i>

04:09.856 --> 04:11.517
&lt;i>That's because he's a great actor.&lt;/i>

04:11.691 --> 04:13.682
Godfather, Rollerball.

04:13.860 --> 04:18.354
&lt;i>Yeah, I can so see these two
kissing in a dorm room.&lt;/i>

04:18.931 --> 04:21.024
That's really sweet,
but I couldn't impose.

04:21.200 --> 04:23.634
- We insist. Right, Charlie?
- Absolutely.

04:24.470 --> 04:27.200
There. You'll come stay with us
for a few days and heal.

04:27.373 --> 04:29.603
- I don't know what to say.
- Say yes.

04:30.143 --> 04:33.408
- Um... Yes.
- Good.

04:33.579 --> 04:35.911
We can go to her apartment
so she can pack a bag.

04:36.082 --> 04:38.778
- Absolutely.
- You'll love Charlie's place.

04:38.951 --> 04:42.045
It's right on the sand,
very quiet, restful.

04:42.221 --> 04:44.416
&lt;i>Dear Penthouse Forum...&lt;/i>

04:45.158 --> 04:47.456
&lt;i>... I always thought
your letters were made up...&lt;/i>

04:47.627 --> 04:50.824
&lt;i>... until my fiancée's roommate
came to stay with us for a few days.&lt;/i>

04:50.997 --> 04:53.557
- Right, Charlie?
- Absolutely.

04:58.571 --> 05:00.266
Hey, Alan?

05:04.010 --> 05:05.534
Alan?

05:05.711 --> 05:07.804
Be right there.

05:10.283 --> 05:11.773
What's up?

05:17.323 --> 05:20.190
- What were you doing?
- Shaving.

05:20.993 --> 05:22.017
At night?

05:22.195 --> 05:24.993
Well, not so much shaving
as trimming.

05:26.466 --> 05:27.831
So how was dinner?

05:29.669 --> 05:30.863
Forget dinner.

05:31.037 --> 05:33.130
Please tell me
you weren't using my razor.

05:33.306 --> 05:35.570
Mine doesn't have the floating heads.

05:36.909 --> 05:39.844
I don't believe you.
I put that thing on my face.

05:40.546 --> 05:42.537
I was gonna clean it
before I gave it back.

05:42.715 --> 05:45.206
I don't want it back.

05:45.384 --> 05:47.852
- Really?
- Yeah, yeah. It's yours.

05:48.054 --> 05:50.181
- Merry Christmas.
- Thank you.

05:50.356 --> 05:52.256
This is just a stocking stuffer, right?

05:52.425 --> 05:54.859
I mean, you are gonna give me
a real present too?

05:55.061 --> 05:56.187
A real present?

05:56.362 --> 05:59.661
Well, you obviously didn't put
much thought into this one.

06:01.434 --> 06:03.868
- Good night, Alan.
- Good night.

06:07.373 --> 06:10.171
Oh, I almost forgot.
Pack up your stuff and get out.

06:11.344 --> 06:14.438
Okay, okay.
The razor can be my Christmas present.

06:14.614 --> 06:19.017
No. Chelsea's girlfriend is staying here,
so you're gonna sleep on the couch.

06:19.185 --> 06:21.415
Why don't you have
Jake sleep on the couch?

06:21.587 --> 06:25.489
Fair question. Why don't you
trim your ball hair with a steak knife?

06:31.464 --> 06:33.830
I feel bad kicking your brother
out of his room.

06:34.000 --> 06:37.231
Well, that's only
because you don't know him.

06:37.803 --> 06:41.204
Here we go. Little chamomile tea,
help you sleep.

06:41.374 --> 06:44.036
Chelsea, I can't thank you enough.

06:44.210 --> 06:47.407
Don't be silly, I know what it feels like
to have my heart broken.

06:47.613 --> 06:49.478
Me too.

06:51.017 --> 06:52.450
You know, theoretically.

06:53.920 --> 06:56.855
- Well, I'm grateful to you both.
- And we're grateful to you.

06:59.358 --> 07:01.758
You know, theoretically.

07:03.396 --> 07:06.058
Tomorrow you can sleep in,
take a nice, long walk on...

07:06.232 --> 07:09.395
&lt;i>I've been
a really good boyfriend tonight.&lt;/i>

07:09.569 --> 07:12.663
&lt;i>Chelsea should do something nice
for me.&lt;/i>

07:13.506 --> 07:15.736
&lt;i>Like make out with Gail.&lt;/i>

07:16.542 --> 07:19.568
Okay, I put fresh sheets on the bed.

07:19.745 --> 07:22.077
Alan, this is my friend Gail.
Gail, this is Alan.

07:22.248 --> 07:25.411
I'm so sorry to put you out like this,
but your brother...

07:25.585 --> 07:28.748
&lt;i>Gorp. Fnark. Schmegle.&lt;/i>

07:30.556 --> 07:33.286
&lt;i>Oh, God, I've been waiting for you
all my life.&lt;/i>

07:34.994 --> 07:37.929
&lt;i>Marry me, have my children.&lt;/i>

07:38.531 --> 07:40.499
It's really very generous of you.

07:41.033 --> 07:44.560
&lt;i>Gorp. Fnark. Schmegle.&lt;/i>

07:45.972 --> 07:48.065
Come on, I'll show you the room.

08:16.636 --> 08:18.604
Chelsea?

08:31.017 --> 08:32.780
Chelsea?

08:37.189 --> 08:38.986
It's gonna be okay.

08:49.001 --> 08:53.370
- Chels, you in there?
It's okay, Charlie. Come on in.

09:00.980 --> 09:03.471
- Everything all right?
- She's pretty upset.

09:03.649 --> 09:06.516
I'm sorry I'm such a basket case.

09:06.686 --> 09:09.985
Oh, please, we're here for you, baby.

09:10.156 --> 09:13.250
- Right, Charlie?
- Absolutely.

09:15.828 --> 09:18.888
I guess I'll leave you two alone.

09:19.532 --> 09:20.726
You don't have to go.

09:24.770 --> 09:26.397
I don't?

09:27.173 --> 09:29.107
Not unless you want to.

09:30.609 --> 09:33.442
&lt;i>Gorp. Fnark. Schmegle.&lt;/i>

09:34.346 --> 09:37.577
Come on, Charlie, we all know
what you really wanna do.

09:37.750 --> 09:39.615
We do?

09:40.553 --> 09:41.679
We do.

09:43.255 --> 09:44.688
Come here, join us.

09:49.495 --> 09:51.554
Uh... Okay.

09:59.672 --> 10:02.698
So, what now?

10:03.676 --> 10:05.473
Do I really need to tell you?

10:05.644 --> 10:08.875
We'd probably be better off
if you did.

10:10.449 --> 10:12.178
Okay.

10:12.451 --> 10:15.113
I want you to make Gail happy.

10:19.325 --> 10:22.988
- And you're onboard?
- It was my idea.

10:23.629 --> 10:25.790
Don't worry,
she and I have done this before.

10:25.965 --> 10:27.398
In college.

10:28.033 --> 10:30.024
I knew it.

10:34.073 --> 10:37.804
Okay, let's turn that frown
upside down.

10:40.045 --> 10:42.513
That's a good boy.

10:43.082 --> 10:44.640
- Hey, Chels?
- Yeah, babe?

10:45.251 --> 10:48.550
- This is a dream, right?
- Of course, it's a dream.

10:48.721 --> 10:51.713
You think I'm really gonna let you sleep
with my best friend?

10:52.958 --> 10:54.892
Well, in that case, hang on...

10:55.060 --> 10:57.893
...because I'm gonna do
some real freaky stuff here.

11:16.182 --> 11:17.615
Yowza.

11:18.751 --> 11:21.948
Excuse me.
I brought you some fresh towels, Gail.

11:22.121 --> 11:24.112
Oh, aren't you sweet.

11:24.290 --> 11:25.985
Sure, sweet.

11:26.158 --> 11:28.251
Go smell his room.

11:30.996 --> 11:33.226
- Morning.
- Good, you're up.

11:33.399 --> 11:35.663
I made you some toast.
Here's your orange juice.

11:35.868 --> 11:38.336
- Oh, thank you, honey.
- I'll see you later.

11:38.504 --> 11:42.668
- Wait, wait, wait. You're leaving?
- I told you I have to go in to work today.

11:42.842 --> 11:46.369
- But what about Gail?
- She can take care of herself.

11:46.545 --> 11:48.570
I think she's already made
a new friend.

11:48.747 --> 11:50.009
Yeah, I saw.

11:50.182 --> 11:52.207
You don't think
he's got a shot, do you?

11:52.384 --> 11:55.285
- Charlie, you're horrible.
- I was joking.

11:55.454 --> 11:57.115
So how long
are you gonna be gone?

11:57.289 --> 12:00.349
I'll be home for dinner.
Thought I'd pick up some Chinese food...

12:00.526 --> 12:01.788
&lt;i>Is she nuts?&lt;/i>

12:01.961 --> 12:03.986
&lt;i>I can't be trusted alone
with that chick.&lt;/i>

12:05.364 --> 12:06.991
&lt;i>Wait, maybe this is a test.&lt;/i>

12:07.166 --> 12:08.190
&lt;i>A trap.&lt;/i>

12:08.400 --> 12:11.767
&lt;i>The two of them are in cahoots
to find out if I'll make a move.&lt;/i>

12:11.937 --> 12:15.338
&lt;i>Cahoots, that's a funny word.&lt;/i>

12:15.674 --> 12:17.505
&lt;i>Sounds like an owl sneezing.&lt;/i>

12:17.676 --> 12:20.372
&lt;i>Ca... Ca... Ca... Cahoots.&lt;/i>

12:20.546 --> 12:23.413
- So I'll call you later.
- Absolutely.

12:25.484 --> 12:28.544
- Morning, Alan.
- Oh, morning.

12:28.721 --> 12:30.188
Thank you for letting
Gail have your room.

12:30.356 --> 12:33.382
&lt;i>Oh, don't be silly. Happy to do it.
Mi casa, her casa.&lt;/i>

12:33.959 --> 12:35.017
Actually it's his...

12:35.194 --> 12:38.095
...but the dehumidifier and the nightlight
belong to me.

12:38.264 --> 12:40.425
Still very nice of you. See you later.

12:42.668 --> 12:44.329
What you got going on today?

12:44.503 --> 12:47.028
Gonna play a little tennis in 1958?

12:48.240 --> 12:51.437
This old thing? This is just
my knock-around clothes.

12:51.610 --> 12:53.840
So, what's the story on Gail?

12:54.013 --> 12:55.776
- Bad breakup?
- Something like that.

12:55.948 --> 12:58.576
- She's on the rebound?
- Where are you going with this?

12:58.751 --> 13:00.514
Nowhere, I'm just curious about her.

13:00.686 --> 13:04.213
And, you know, when we met last night,
I sensed a little spark between us.

13:04.390 --> 13:08.190
If there was a spark, it's only
because she was warming up her Taser.

13:09.395 --> 13:10.862
Ha, ha. Very funny.

13:11.030 --> 13:14.796
The only way you're gonna hook up
with someone like Gail is in your dreams.

13:14.967 --> 13:16.491
Already did.

13:17.570 --> 13:19.060
- Really? Was Chelsea there?
- No.

13:19.238 --> 13:21.365
Good lord, how creepy would that be?

13:24.276 --> 13:26.107
Well, regardless, forget about Gail.

13:26.278 --> 13:29.042
Potato head out there
has a better shot than you do.

13:29.982 --> 13:32.576
I've got a nephew about your age.
You should meet him.

13:32.751 --> 13:35.242
He plays guitar,
maybe you guys could jam sometime.

13:35.421 --> 13:37.116
&lt;i>Oh, boobies.&lt;/i>

13:41.327 --> 13:44.296
There is a very good chance
that a woman like that...

13:44.496 --> 13:46.794
...is tired of rich, handsome,
successful guys...

13:46.999 --> 13:49.160
...who have homes
and recently-built cars.

13:49.335 --> 13:53.101
- You really believe that?
- I have to.

13:53.806 --> 13:57.401
- Woof. Who's that?
- Chelsea's friend.

13:57.576 --> 14:01.103
She's going through a bad breakup
so she's gonna stay here for a few days.

14:01.280 --> 14:03.145
&lt;i>Too bad I prefer the fellas.&lt;/i>

14:05.684 --> 14:08.414
&lt;i>Then again, I could always
draw a mustache on her.&lt;/i>

14:23.168 --> 14:24.795
Alan?

14:25.404 --> 14:27.099
Jake?

14:27.740 --> 14:29.469
Berta?

14:31.844 --> 14:33.835
Oh, boy.

14:35.047 --> 14:37.038
Although,
maybe this is another dream.

14:45.958 --> 14:48.358
- Gail, you okay?
I'm fine.

14:48.560 --> 14:50.653
Good, good.

14:50.829 --> 14:53.957
I'm gonna run some errands.
Can I get you anything while I'm out?

14:54.133 --> 14:56.601
A reason to live.

14:58.804 --> 15:00.567
Alrighty.

15:07.212 --> 15:08.839
Coming in.

15:11.483 --> 15:13.144
Sorry.

15:13.318 --> 15:15.309
I just got some bad news.

15:15.487 --> 15:16.818
What happened?

15:16.989 --> 15:19.719
- My boyfriend...
- Rufus?

15:19.892 --> 15:21.883
That's my dog.

15:22.061 --> 15:26.361
- Oh, yeah. He's okay, right?
- He's fine.

15:26.532 --> 15:29.592
I just found out
Brian is already seeing someone else.

15:29.768 --> 15:30.894
No.

15:31.070 --> 15:34.665
I mean, we just broke up and he's
already sleeping with another woman?

15:34.840 --> 15:36.740
The pig.

15:38.010 --> 15:40.501
I thought we had something.

15:40.746 --> 15:42.543
He always said I was his soul mate...

15:42.715 --> 15:45.149
...and that he wanted
to spend his life with me.

15:45.317 --> 15:46.875
&lt;i>This can't be a dream.&lt;/i>

15:47.052 --> 15:49.418
&lt;i>She's still got her clothes on.&lt;/i>

15:49.621 --> 15:51.885
&lt;i>And she's talking.&lt;/i>

15:52.891 --> 15:57.419
- Why can't I find a nice guy like you?
- Absolutely.

15:58.564 --> 16:00.555
Maybe Chelsea
would let me borrow you.

16:06.004 --> 16:08.131
Excuse me, gotta pee.

16:10.642 --> 16:12.940
Oh, crap, crap, crap.

16:13.145 --> 16:15.375
- Here you go.
- Thanks.

16:16.682 --> 16:18.741
I don't know how much longer
I can hold out.

16:18.917 --> 16:20.544
I hear you.

16:21.754 --> 16:23.722
- What?
- Nothing.

16:25.524 --> 16:28.891
I gotta get Gail out of here
before I do something I'm gonna regret.

16:29.061 --> 16:31.928
You know, after I thoroughly enjoy it.

16:33.165 --> 16:34.393
Just tell her to leave.

16:34.566 --> 16:37.057
I can't do that,
she's Chelsea's best friend.

16:37.236 --> 16:38.669
They were college roommates.

16:38.837 --> 16:40.668
Really?

16:41.406 --> 16:44.569
- You think they experimented?
- Oh, yeah.

16:51.683 --> 16:54.618
I gotta figure out a way
to get Gail to leave on her own.

16:54.787 --> 16:58.348
- You got the perfect tool for the job.
- What are you talking about?

16:58.524 --> 17:01.925
The one tool that's guaranteed
to drive any woman out of your house.

17:02.094 --> 17:03.561
Hello.

17:06.098 --> 17:08.259
Oh, look, it's an Allen wrench.

17:12.604 --> 17:15.072
What was that about?
- Nothing. Nothing.

17:15.240 --> 17:19.142
I was just telling Berta that I was wrong
about you not having a shot with Gail.

17:19.311 --> 17:22.144
Why, did she say something?
Did she ask about me?

17:22.314 --> 17:25.306
How about a double wedding?
As long as you're paying for one.

17:26.618 --> 17:29.416
Slow down. Slow down.
Nobody said anything.

17:29.588 --> 17:31.579
I just realized
I might've been jealous...

17:31.757 --> 17:33.281
...because she's so beautiful...

17:33.458 --> 17:36.188
...and I can't have her,
I didn't want you to have her.

17:36.361 --> 17:38.386
Yeah, I was thinking it might be that.

17:39.965 --> 17:43.162
Anyway, it's not fair for me
to stand in the way of your happiness.

17:43.335 --> 17:46.202
I always thought
that was one of your favorite things.

17:46.371 --> 17:48.703
Do you wanna pick nits
or go talk to a woman...

17:48.874 --> 17:52.207
...who's vulnerable and may very well
be looking for revenge sex?

17:52.377 --> 17:55.107
I don't want revenge sex,
I want a loving relationship...

17:55.280 --> 17:58.579
...that has depth and meaning
and will withstand the test of time.

17:58.750 --> 18:00.980
Oh, that's good. I'd lead with that.

18:01.620 --> 18:03.986
- You think?
- Oh, yeah, go get her.

18:04.523 --> 18:06.684
All right. All right. Wish me luck.

18:06.859 --> 18:07.883
You don't need luck.

18:08.060 --> 18:11.188
You've got the exact skills
needed to get this job done.

18:11.363 --> 18:13.228
Thanks, Charlie.
You're a good brother.

18:14.700 --> 18:17.999
&lt;i>If he actually gets laid,
I'm gonna hang myself.&lt;/i>

18:20.572 --> 18:22.130
Come in.

18:23.475 --> 18:25.340
- Hey, there.
- Hi, Alan.

18:25.911 --> 18:29.278
- You up for a little company?
- I guess.

18:31.917 --> 18:34.351
You know, it does get easier.

18:34.519 --> 18:36.419
The wound does heal.

18:36.588 --> 18:38.385
I know. Thank you.

18:38.557 --> 18:40.115
It may not feel like it now...

18:40.292 --> 18:43.728
...but before too long, you'll forget
about that fellow who hurt you...

18:43.896 --> 18:47.730
...because another fellow
will be in your heart.

18:47.900 --> 18:49.595
A fellow who will never hurt you...

18:51.203 --> 18:53.330
...who will never leave your side.

18:53.906 --> 18:58.275
A fellow who wants nothing
more than to love you.

18:58.443 --> 19:00.707
&lt;i>Oh, dear God, no.&lt;/i>

19:03.815 --> 19:06.443
Thanks for your hospitality,
but I should get back home.

19:06.618 --> 19:08.347
- Anytime.
- So where'd we leave it?

19:08.520 --> 19:11.045
- I'll call you, you'll call me?
- I'll call you.

19:14.026 --> 19:17.553
So how'd it go?

19:19.031 --> 19:21.056
You heard her. She's gonna call me.

19:29.808 --> 19:31.776
Shame on you, Alan Harper.

19:31.944 --> 19:34.606
You knew that Gail
was going through a difficult time.

19:34.780 --> 19:37.943
What do you do? You try
to take advantage, to exploit her...

19:38.116 --> 19:41.745
&lt;i>What is it about an angry woman
that I find so hot?&lt;/i>

19:43.622 --> 19:45.852
&lt;i>Even when that fat cashier
was yelling at me...&lt;/i>

19:46.024 --> 19:48.015
&lt;i>... I got a little engorged.&lt;/i>

19:49.628 --> 19:52.825
&lt;i>Boy, if I could just find
somebody like Chelsea.&lt;/i>

19:52.998 --> 19:54.556
&lt;i>I mean, look at her go.&lt;/i>

19:55.667 --> 19:57.931
&lt;i>She's a real fireball.&lt;/i>

19:59.204 --> 20:01.695
&lt;i>Speaking of fireballs,
next time I manscape...&lt;/i>

20:01.873 --> 20:04.501
&lt;i>... I should probably skip
the aftershave.&lt;/i>
